      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawthorn%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "From 1899 to 1920, Hawthorn hosted the Hawthorn Pottery Company, one of the Redbank Valley’s leading small industries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.usacitiesonline.com/pacountyhawthorn.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A railroad siding was later added to serve the pottery, linking Hawthorn to the regional rail network.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.usacitiesonline.com/pacountyhawthorn.htm"
    },
    {
